				<string>SPIKE 010 -- NUMBER COERCION AT A DIRECT SET-ACTION PARAMETER

ONE question: is the Number coercion correct on a Set Brightness operand -- a
DIRECT action parameter -- as opposed to the If-condition operand position that
Donor 4.1 already confirms?

Standalone. Reads no state file, references no production shortcut, needs no
Personal Automation. Safe to run: it captures the current brightness BEFORE it
writes anything, and restores it at the end.

PRIMARY observation is the EDITOR, not the run: compare leg A's operand chip
against leg B's. Leg B is deliberately uncoerced. That is the control, not a bug.</string>
			</dict>
